Termux:VA daemon encoder changes, paired with
android-vaapi's 0100-termux-va-encode.patch:
- retry configuration without "low-latency", which ACodec rejects for OMX
  encoders such as OMX.qcom.video.encoder.avc on Snapdragon 855;
- ENC_UNIT_FORCE_KEY requests a sync frame for that picture, and
  ENC_UNIT_SET_BITRATE changes the target mid-stream; the encoder's own
  key-frame period is long, since VA-API clients choose picture types;
- parameter sets precede every sync frame;
- hardware encoders are listed in "<socket>.encoders", and Android's software
  encoders are refused.

--- a/common/tva_protocol.h
+++ b/common/tva_protocol.h
@@ -153,6 +153,16 @@
  * unchanged; both endpoints must be updated for raw frames over 8 MiB. */
 #define MAX_ENCODE_FRAME (16 * 1024 * 1024)
 
+/* Encoder uplink controls in the high bits of the length word, which a raw
+ * frame (at most MAX_ENCODE_FRAME) never sets.  VA-API clients choose the
+ * picture types, and WebRTC changes its target rate and asks for key frames
+ * at any time, so these follow each picture:
+ *   FORCE_KEY    this frame must be coded as a sync frame (IDR / key frame);
+ *   SET_BITRATE  a 4-byte big-endian target bitrate follows instead of a
+ *                frame, and no packet is returned for it. */
+#define ENC_UNIT_FORCE_KEY   0x80000000u
+#define ENC_UNIT_SET_BITRATE 0x40000000u
+
 /* Max concurrent decode sessions the daemon accepts (hardware supports 16). */
 #define MAX_CLIENTS 8
 
